1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:01,960
Does a slinky's
bottom fall?

2
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:02,900
Not yet.

3
00:00:03,353 --> 00:00:05,908
Held by the top,
a slinky hangs long

4
00:00:05,908 --> 00:00:06,953
and still.

5
00:00:06,953 --> 00:00:07,978
Let go.

6
00:00:08,208 --> 00:00:09,053
The top drops…

7
00:00:09,053 --> 00:00:11,203
and the bottom
doesn't move at all.

8
00:00:14,525 --> 00:00:17,035
Slowed down,
the top coils pile up

9
00:00:17,035 --> 00:00:19,975
from above, while
the bottom floats there.

10
00:00:19,975 --> 00:00:22,190
For about three tenths
of a second.

11
00:00:22,353 --> 00:00:23,793
Why doesn't it fall?

12
00:00:23,833 --> 00:00:25,968
Nothing down there
has been told.

13
00:00:26,223 --> 00:00:27,958
The pull of the spring
doesn't jump

14
00:00:27,958 --> 00:00:30,678
to the other end; it
travels down the coils,

15
00:00:30,678 --> 00:00:31,968
like a wave.

16
00:00:32,173 --> 00:00:35,173
Until the news arrives,
the bottom has no reason

17
00:00:35,173 --> 00:00:35,953
to move.

18
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:39,145
Its balance point,

19
00:00:39,145 --> 00:00:41,230
the spot you could
balance it on?

20
00:00:41,230 --> 00:00:43,245
It falls like
a dropped ball.

21
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:45,790
The top rushes,
the bottom waits:

22
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:47,805
the average
is a plain fall.

23
00:00:50,887 --> 00:00:54,317
Measure it: the bottom's
ghosts stack in one place

24
00:00:54,317 --> 00:00:56,222
for three tenths
of a second.

25
00:00:56,297 --> 00:00:59,417
Then the top arrives,
and they all go together.

26
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:01,500
Even through a spring,

27
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,755
news travels
at a limited speed.

28
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:07,720
Next: dry spaghetti,
bent until it snaps.

29
00:01:07,890 --> 00:01:09,410
It almost never breaks
in two.
